# 🔍 Network Port Scanner

**A fast, multi-threaded TCP port scanner written in pure Python.**

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.8%2B-3776AB?logo=python&logoColor=white)
![Release](https://img.shields.io/github/v/release/jo-123456/network-port-scanner)
![License](https://img.shields.io/github/license/jo-123456/network-port-scanner)
![Dependencies](https://img.shields.io/badge/dependencies-none-brightgreen)

</div>

Scan a host for open ports, identify common services, read simple banners, and get a clean results table with a summary. It uses only the Python standard library, so there is nothing to install.

> ⚠️ **Legal notice:** Only scan machines you own or have explicit written permission to test. Unauthorized port scanning may be illegal.

